# Unified-Field Solver — Architecture Notes

This document describes the internal architecture of the solver as implemented
in the Experimental Analysis Phase.

## 1. Ingestion Layer
- Loads Planck CMB maps (HEALPix)
- Loads SDSS galaxy density fields
- Converts all inputs into scalar fields T_obs(x)

## 2. Harmonic-Relaxation Solver
Solves:

    ∇²T_sim = 1 / (2λ)

on the sphere using spherical-harmonic decomposition.

## 3. Residual Isolation Engine
Computes:

    ΔT(x) = |T_obs(x) - T_sim(x)|

Outputs:
- residual map
- non-Gaussianity metrics
- clustering diagnostics

## 4. Power Spectrum Module
Computes P_ΔT(ℓ) and compares to:
- ΛCDM predictions
- Planck noise simulations
- null-test splits

## 5. Integrity Layer
Includes:
- XOR memory cipher
- quantum-resistant hash
- Noether conservation audit (0.0001% threshold)

## 6. Dark-Sector Interpretation
Maps ΔT into:
- ψ_DM (dark-matter residual clustering)
- Λ_DE (dark-energy expansion-bias vectors)